// From the law's annex on the flag, Official Gazette 67/1994, pages 3718 and 3719:
//   width to length 1:2, three bands of a third each, here 40 on a 120 by 240 grid
//   the arms' center is at 1/4 of the length (60) and on the line between white and blue (40)
//   the arms are 1/3 of the width high (40), half in the white and half in the blue
// The shapes are from the Commons drawing, on the same grid: from 20 to 60 high, centered at 60.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Slovenia"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
  adapted-from "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovenia_(Pantone).svg" {
    author "Wikimedia Commons contributors, listed in the file's history"
    license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
    part "the coat of arms"
  }
  source "https://www.uradni-list.si/_pdf/1994/Ur/u1994067.pdf"
  source "https://www.gov.si/en/topics/national-symbols/"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/si.html"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Slovenia_(Pantone).svg"
  note "The proportion, bands, and the arms' size and place are from the law's annex, which is part of the law under its Article 4."
  note "The law defines the arms by an annexed drawing and geometric rule. The drawing here comes from the Commons file and isn't from the law."
  note "The SCOTDIC codes are the law's. The CMYK values are from the government's page on the symbols, not the law. The hex and Pantone values are the Album des Pavillons 2023's, as reported by FOTW, and aren't legal."
  note "Commons' author field names Republic of Slovenia, which appears to be who made the design or passed the law rather than who drew this file."
  law "Act on the Coat of Arms, Flag and Anthem of the Republic of Slovenia and on the Slovene National Flag, Official Gazette 67/1994" {
    source "https://www.uradni-list.si/_pdf/1994/Ur/u1994067.pdf"
  }
  restriction "Article 8 of the law: the arms, the flag and the Slovene national flag can't be protected as a trademark, model or pattern, or used to mark goods or services, except for collective marks held by ministries or the government." {
    source "https://www.uradni-list.si/_pdf/1994/Ur/u1994067.pdf"
  }
}
